{"module":"colonizers","voice":"female","duration":375.4,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Los colonizadores: Portugal, España, Gran Bretaña y el sistema imperial","start":0.0,"end":5.89,"words":[[0.08,0.32],[0.32,1.43],[1.71,2.43],[2.7,3.26],[3.54,3.86],[3.86,4.41],[4.41,4.49],[4.49,4.65],[4.65,5.21],[5.21,5.85]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Colón fue una persona dentro de un sistema que funcionó durante cuatro siglos.","start":6.69,"end":11.33,"words":[[6.78,7.1],[7.1,7.29],[7.29,7.49],[7.49,7.94],[7.94,8.33],[8.33,8.45],[8.45,8.58],[8.58,9.04],[9.04,9.17],[9.17,9.68],[9.68,10.13],[10.13,10.52],[10.52,10.97]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Cada imperio añadió una pieza a la maquinaria: el comercio, la teoría legal, el código de plantación, las categorías raciales.","start":11.68,"end":20.91,"words":[[11.72,12.01],[12.01,12.51],[12.51,12.93],[12.93,13.15],[13.15,13.51],[13.51,13.58],[13.58,13.72],[13.72,14.43],[14.68,14.83],[14.83,15.47],[15.72,15.86],[15.86,16.36],[16.36,16.79],[17.04,17.18],[17.18,17.61],[17.61,17.75],[17.75,18.54],[18.79,19.0],[19.0,19.79],[19.79,20.43]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Juntos construyeron el mundo al que la Ley CAREN todavía responde.","start":21.26,"end":25.28,"words":[[21.35,21.73],[21.73,22.49],[22.49,22.62],[22.62,22.93],[22.93,23.06],[23.06,23.19],[23.19,23.31],[23.31,23.5],[23.5,23.82],[23.82,24.33],[24.33,24.89]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Portugal abre la trata atlántica","start":25.63,"end":28.37,"words":[[25.74,26.48],[26.48,26.84],[26.84,27.03],[27.03,27.49],[27.49,28.32]]},{"el":"s0","text":"En 1444, en Lagos (Portugal), unos 235 africanos cautivos fueron repartidos y vendidos en una plaza pública, un hecho que el cronista real Gomes Eanes de Zurara describió en detalle.","start":29.07,"end":43.39,"words":[[29.15,29.28],[29.28,31.43],[31.66,31.8],[31.8,32.13],[32.13,32.74],[32.97,33.24],[33.24,34.78],[34.78,35.39],[35.39,35.92],[35.92,36.32],[36.32,37.0],[37.0,37.06],[37.06,37.6],[37.6,37.73],[37.73,37.93],[37.93,38.27],[38.27,38.81],[39.04,39.18],[39.18,39.44],[39.44,39.58],[39.58,39.71],[39.71,40.25],[40.25,40.52],[40.52,40.85],[40.85,41.19],[41.19,41.32],[41.32,41.72],[41.72,42.33],[42.33,42.46],[42.46,43.0]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Portugal construyó el castillo de Elmina en 1482 y comerció a lo largo de la costa africana.","start":43.74,"end":50.92,"words":[[43.83,44.38],[44.38,44.99],[44.99,45.12],[45.12,45.66],[45.66,45.8],[45.8,46.2],[46.2,46.34],[46.34,48.17],[48.17,48.24],[48.24,48.78],[48.78,48.85],[48.85,48.98],[48.98,49.32],[49.32,49.46],[49.46,49.59],[49.59,49.93],[49.93,50.54]]},{"el":"s0","text":"En 1526, el rey Afonso I del Congo, él mismo cristiano y aliado de Portugal, escribió al rey de Portugal para protestar porque los traficantes secuestraban a su pueblo, “incluso a nobles e hijos de nobles”.","start":51.27,"end":66.48,"words":[[51.36,51.51],[51.51,53.2],[53.46,53.61],[53.61,53.83],[53.83,54.28],[54.28,54.35],[54.35,54.57],[54.57,55.01],[55.27,55.42],[55.42,55.79],[55.79,56.45],[56.45,56.53],[56.53,56.97],[56.97,57.12],[57.12,57.78],[58.04,58.63],[58.63,58.78],[58.78,59.0],[59.0,59.15],[59.15,59.74],[59.74,60.04],[60.04,60.7],[60.7,61.07],[61.07,61.29],[61.29,62.1],[62.1,62.99],[62.99,63.06],[63.06,63.21],[63.21,63.73],[63.99,64.5],[64.5,64.58],[64.58,65.02],[65.02,65.1],[65.1,65.39],[65.39,65.54],[65.54,66.06]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Los barcos portugueses y brasileños llevaron a través del Atlántico a unos 5.8 millones de africanos, más que cualquier otra nación.","start":66.83,"end":76.38,"words":[[66.93,67.15],[67.15,67.59],[67.59,68.33],[68.33,68.4],[68.4,69.14],[69.14,69.66],[69.66,69.73],[69.73,70.17],[70.17,70.4],[70.4,71.06],[71.06,71.13],[71.13,71.43],[71.43,72.46],[72.46,73.05],[73.05,73.2],[73.2,73.94],[74.2,74.42],[74.42,74.57],[74.57,75.16],[75.16,75.45],[75.45,75.97]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Brasil fue el mayor destino y el último país de América en abolir la esclavitud, en 1888.","start":76.73,"end":84.78,"words":[[76.79,77.25],[77.25,77.48],[77.48,77.63],[77.63,78.01],[78.01,78.54],[78.54,78.62],[78.62,78.77],[78.77,79.22],[79.22,79.53],[79.53,79.68],[79.68,80.21],[80.21,80.36],[80.36,80.82],[80.82,80.97],[80.97,81.81],[82.07,82.23],[82.23,84.35]]},{"el":"h1","text":"España se pregunta si los indígenas son plenamente humanos","start":85.68,"end":89.52,"words":[[85.77,86.22],[86.22,86.37],[86.37,86.98],[86.98,87.13],[87.13,87.35],[87.35,88.03],[88.03,88.26],[88.26,89.02],[89.02,89.47]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Desde 1513, los conquistadores españoles leían en voz alta el Requerimiento, en español, a pueblos que no podían entenderlo, exigiendo sumisión a la Corona y a la Iglesia y declarando que cualquier muerte resultante sería culpa de ellos.","start":90.22,"end":107.13,"words":[[90.32,90.68],[90.68,91.99],[92.24,92.46],[92.46,93.4],[93.4,94.05],[94.05,94.49],[94.49,94.63],[94.63,94.85],[94.85,95.14],[95.14,95.29],[95.29,96.23],[96.48,96.63],[96.63,97.21],[97.46,97.53],[97.53,98.04],[98.04,98.18],[98.18,98.33],[98.33,98.84],[98.84,99.63],[99.89,100.61],[100.61,101.19],[101.19,101.27],[101.27,101.41],[101.41,101.85],[101.85,101.92],[101.92,101.99],[101.99,102.13],[102.13,102.64],[102.64,102.71],[102.71,103.44],[103.44,103.58],[103.58,104.16],[104.16,104.6],[104.6,105.32],[105.32,105.76],[105.76,106.12],[106.12,106.27],[106.27,106.7]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Los indígenas eran asignados a españoles como trabajadores forzados bajo la encomienda.","start":107.48,"end":112.98,"words":[[107.55,107.74],[107.74,108.34],[108.34,108.6],[108.6,109.2],[109.2,109.27],[109.27,109.86],[109.86,110.13],[110.13,110.92],[110.92,111.45],[111.45,111.71],[111.71,111.85],[111.85,112.57]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Bartolomé de las Casas, antiguo encomendero convertido en fraile, pasó cincuenta años denunciándola; las Leyes Nuevas de 1542 la limitaron.","start":113.33,"end":124.15,"words":[[113.39,114.01],[114.01,114.15],[114.15,114.35],[114.35,114.77],[115.01,115.49],[115.49,116.25],[116.25,116.93],[116.93,117.07],[117.07,117.55],[117.79,118.07],[118.07,118.69],[118.69,118.97],[118.97,119.93],[120.17,120.38],[120.38,120.72],[120.72,121.13],[121.13,121.27],[121.27,122.92],[122.92,123.06],[123.06,123.75]]},{"el":"s1","text":"En la Junta de Valladolid (1550–51), Las Casas discutió con Juan Ginés de Sepúlveda, quien sostenía, citando a Aristóteles, que los indígenas eran “siervos por naturaleza”.","start":124.5,"end":137.79,"words":[[124.63,124.77],[124.77,124.9],[124.9,125.25],[125.25,125.39],[125.39,126.07],[126.07,128.62],[128.86,129.07],[129.07,129.41],[129.41,129.96],[129.96,130.17],[130.17,130.45],[130.45,130.79],[130.79,130.93],[130.93,131.62],[131.86,132.13],[132.13,132.82],[133.06,133.54],[133.54,133.61],[133.61,134.44],[134.68,134.82],[134.82,135.02],[135.02,135.64],[135.64,135.92],[135.92,136.4],[136.4,136.61],[136.61,137.37]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Más tarde, las colonias españolas clasificaron a las personas en decenas de castas de ascendencia mixta, registradas en pinturas oficiales.","start":138.14,"end":147.01,"words":[[138.22,138.42],[138.42,138.82],[139.05,139.25],[139.25,139.78],[139.78,140.37],[140.37,141.17],[141.17,141.23],[141.23,141.43],[141.43,141.96],[141.96,142.09],[142.09,142.55],[142.55,142.69],[142.69,143.08],[143.08,143.22],[143.22,143.88],[143.88,144.34],[144.57,145.3],[145.3,145.43],[145.43,145.96],[145.96,146.62]]},{"el":"h2","text":"¿Dónde empezó la “raza”?","start":147.91,"end":149.47,"words":[[147.97,148.28],[148.28,148.64],[148.64,148.76],[148.76,149.07]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Algunos historiadores rastrean la raza moderna hasta los estatutos españoles de limpieza de sangre, que desde el siglo XV excluían de ciertos cargos a personas con antepasados judíos o musulmanes incluso después de convertirse, haciendo de la ascendencia, y no de la fe, la prueba.","start":150.17,"end":168.56,"words":[[150.25,150.75],[150.75,151.6],[151.6,152.17],[152.17,152.31],[152.31,152.59],[152.59,153.09],[153.09,153.37],[153.37,153.59],[153.59,154.23],[154.23,154.87],[154.87,155.01],[155.01,155.58],[155.58,155.72],[155.72,156.22],[156.46,156.61],[156.61,156.96],[156.96,157.1],[157.1,157.46],[157.46,157.81],[157.81,158.53],[158.53,158.67],[158.67,159.16],[159.16,159.59],[159.59,159.66],[159.66,160.23],[160.23,160.44],[160.44,161.22],[161.22,161.72],[161.72,161.79],[161.79,162.5],[162.5,163.0],[163.0,163.5],[163.5,163.64],[163.64,164.49],[164.74,165.24],[165.24,165.38],[165.38,165.52],[165.52,166.3],[166.55,166.62],[166.62,166.77],[166.77,166.91],[166.91,167.05],[167.05,167.26],[167.51,167.65],[167.65,168.15]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Otros ven surgir la raza sobre todo de la esclavitud atlántica y del derecho colonial inglés.","start":168.91,"end":174.96,"words":[[169.0,169.35],[169.35,169.57],[169.57,170.0],[170.0,170.14],[170.14,170.42],[170.42,170.78],[170.78,171.07],[171.07,171.21],[171.21,171.35],[171.35,172.06],[172.06,172.71],[172.71,172.78],[172.78,172.99],[172.99,173.49],[173.49,174.06],[174.06,174.56]]},{"el":"s2","text":"La mayoría coincide en que se formó entre 1450 y 1700, que es el argumento del módulo “Antes de la raza”.","start":175.31,"end":183.36,"words":[[175.41,175.54],[175.54,176.06],[176.06,176.58],[176.58,176.71],[176.71,176.84],[176.84,176.97],[176.97,177.29],[177.29,177.62],[177.62,179.24],[179.24,179.31],[179.31,180.29],[180.51,180.64],[180.64,180.77],[180.77,180.9],[180.9,181.49],[181.49,181.68],[181.68,182.07],[182.07,182.4],[182.4,182.53],[182.53,182.66],[182.66,182.98]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Gran Bretaña escribe el código de plantación","start":184.26,"end":187.31,"words":[[184.38,184.69],[184.69,185.22],[185.22,185.75],[185.75,185.9],[185.9,186.36],[186.36,186.51],[186.51,187.27]]},{"el":"s3","text":"John Hawkins encabezó los primeros viajes esclavistas de Inglaterra en la década de 1560, más tarde con el respaldo de la reina Isabel I.","start":188.01,"end":197.45,"words":[[188.1,188.3],[188.3,188.72],[188.72,189.27],[189.27,189.48],[189.48,190.03],[190.03,190.45],[190.45,191.21],[191.21,191.35],[191.35,191.97],[191.97,192.11],[192.11,192.24],[192.24,192.66],[192.66,192.8],[192.8,194.18],[194.42,194.63],[194.63,194.98],[194.98,195.18],[195.18,195.32],[195.32,195.87],[195.87,196.01],[196.01,196.15],[196.15,196.5],[196.5,196.91],[196.91,197.05]]},{"el":"s3","text":"La Royal African Company, fundada bajo el futuro Jacobo II, transportó más africanos esclavizados que cualquier otra compañía; a muchos los marcaban con “DY” por el duque de York.","start":197.8,"end":210.22,"words":[[197.93,198.07],[198.07,198.45],[198.45,198.97],[198.97,199.57],[199.83,200.36],[200.36,200.66],[200.66,200.81],[200.81,201.25],[201.25,201.7],[201.7,202.0],[202.26,203.01],[203.01,203.24],[203.24,203.91],[203.91,204.81],[204.81,204.96],[204.96,205.56],[205.56,205.86],[205.86,206.6],[206.87,206.94],[206.94,207.39],[207.39,207.61],[207.61,208.21],[208.21,208.44],[208.44,208.59],[208.59,208.81],[208.81,208.96],[208.96,209.26],[209.26,209.41],[209.41,209.78]]},{"el":"s3","text":"El código de esclavos de Barbados de 1661 se convirtió en el modelo de los de Jamaica y Carolina del Sur.","start":210.57,"end":217.92,"words":[[210.69,210.82],[210.82,211.2],[211.2,211.33],[211.33,211.84],[211.84,211.97],[211.97,212.48],[212.48,212.61],[212.61,214.27],[214.27,214.4],[214.4,214.98],[214.98,215.11],[215.11,215.24],[215.24,215.62],[215.62,215.75],[215.75,215.94],[215.94,216.07],[216.07,216.52],[216.52,216.58],[216.58,217.09],[217.09,217.29],[217.29,217.54]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Los barcos británicos llevaron en total a unos 3.2 millones de africanos.","start":218.27,"end":223.48,"words":[[218.38,218.58],[218.58,218.98],[218.98,219.66],[219.66,220.13],[220.13,220.26],[220.26,220.6],[220.6,220.67],[220.67,220.94],[220.94,221.74],[221.74,222.28],[222.28,222.42],[222.42,223.09]]},{"el":"s3","text":"En 1781, la tripulación del barco negrero Zong arrojó por la borda a unos 130 cautivos, y los dueños demandaron a sus aseguradoras por la pérdida como si fuera “carga”.","start":223.83,"end":235.95,"words":[[223.92,224.05],[224.05,225.86],[226.09,226.23],[226.23,226.96],[226.96,227.16],[227.16,227.5],[227.5,227.96],[227.96,228.16],[228.16,228.5],[228.5,228.7],[228.7,228.83],[228.83,229.17],[229.17,229.23],[229.23,229.5],[229.5,230.37],[230.37,230.97],[231.2,231.27],[231.27,231.47],[231.47,231.87],[231.87,232.54],[232.54,232.61],[232.61,232.81],[232.81,233.61],[233.61,233.81],[233.81,233.94],[233.94,234.41],[234.41,234.68],[234.68,234.81],[234.81,235.15],[235.15,235.55]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Los primeros africanos en la Virginia inglesa llegaron en 1619 a bordo del White Lion, un corsario inglés que los había capturado de un barco portugués que transportaba cautivos de Angola.","start":236.3,"end":249.58,"words":[[236.39,236.61],[236.61,237.18],[237.18,237.83],[237.83,237.97],[237.97,238.12],[238.12,238.69],[238.69,239.2],[239.2,239.7],[239.7,239.85],[239.85,241.57],[241.57,241.65],[241.65,242.01],[242.01,242.22],[242.22,242.51],[242.51,242.94],[243.19,243.34],[243.34,243.91],[243.91,244.35],[244.35,244.49],[244.49,244.71],[244.71,245.07],[245.07,245.71],[245.71,245.86],[245.86,246.0],[246.0,246.36],[246.36,246.94],[246.94,247.08],[247.08,247.95],[247.95,248.52],[248.52,248.67],[248.67,249.17]]},{"el":"h4","text":"Francia y los Países Bajos","start":250.48,"end":252.54,"words":[[250.57,251.17],[251.17,251.25],[251.25,251.51],[251.51,252.02],[252.02,252.45]]},{"el":"s4","text":"La Compañía Neerlandesa de las Indias Occidentales comerció africanos esclavizados hacia América y usó mano de obra esclavizada en Nueva Ámsterdam (Nueva York).","start":253.24,"end":263.03,"words":[[253.34,253.47],[253.47,254.09],[254.09,254.84],[254.84,254.97],[254.97,255.18],[255.18,255.59],[255.59,256.41],[256.41,256.95],[256.95,257.57],[257.57,258.39],[258.39,258.66],[258.66,259.14],[259.14,259.2],[259.2,259.41],[259.41,259.68],[259.68,259.82],[259.82,260.09],[260.09,260.84],[260.84,260.98],[260.98,261.32],[261.32,261.93],[261.93,262.27],[262.27,262.61]]},{"el":"s4","text":"El Code Noir de Francia (1685) regía sus colonias; Saint-Domingue, hoy Haití, se convirtió en la colonia más rentable del mundo gracias al trabajo de africanos esclavizados, hasta que derrocaron a los franceses (ver “Antes de la raza” y “Un sistema mundial”).","start":263.38,"end":280.44,"words":[[263.48,263.62],[263.62,263.89],[263.89,264.16],[264.16,264.3],[264.3,264.77],[264.77,266.6],[266.84,267.24],[267.24,267.45],[267.45,268.06],[268.29,269.18],[269.41,269.55],[269.55,269.89],[270.12,270.26],[270.26,270.87],[270.87,271.0],[271.0,271.14],[271.14,271.61],[271.61,271.82],[271.82,272.36],[272.36,272.56],[272.56,272.9],[272.9,273.38],[273.38,273.51],[273.51,273.98],[273.98,274.12],[274.12,274.73],[274.73,275.61],[275.85,276.12],[276.12,276.25],[276.25,276.86],[276.86,276.93],[276.93,277.13],[277.13,277.74],[277.74,277.95],[277.95,278.29],[278.29,278.42],[278.42,278.56],[278.56,278.83],[278.83,278.9],[278.9,279.03],[279.03,279.51],[279.51,280.05]]},{"el":"h5","text":"Estados Unidos se convierte en imperio","start":281.34,"end":283.88,"words":[[281.43,281.94],[281.94,282.38],[282.38,282.53],[282.53,283.19],[283.19,283.33],[283.33,283.85]]},{"el":"s5","text":"En 1893, empresarios estadounidenses respaldados por marines de EE. UU. derrocaron a la reina Liliʻuokalani de Hawái; el Congreso pidió perdón formalmente en 1993.","start":284.58,"end":301.19,"words":[[284.66,284.81],[284.81,286.77],[287.03,287.82],[287.82,288.91],[288.91,289.71],[289.71,289.93],[289.93,290.44],[290.44,290.59],[290.59,290.8],[291.17,291.38],[291.75,292.4],[292.4,292.47],[292.47,292.62],[292.62,292.98],[292.98,295.6],[295.6,295.74],[295.74,296.11],[296.36,296.51],[296.51,297.09],[297.09,297.45],[297.45,297.89],[297.89,298.69],[298.69,298.83],[298.83,300.79]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Después de 1898, EE. UU. tomó Puerto Rico, Guam y Filipinas.","start":301.54,"end":308.47,"words":[[301.64,302.13],[302.13,302.27],[302.27,304.24],[304.49,304.7],[305.05,305.26],[305.61,305.89],[305.89,306.32],[306.32,306.67],[306.91,307.2],[307.2,307.27],[307.27,307.97]]},{"el":"s5","text":"El poema de Rudyard Kipling “La carga del hombre blanco” (1899) instaba a los estadounidenses a gobernar Filipinas, donde una guerra contra los independentistas mató a cientos de miles de filipinos según la mayoría de las estimaciones.","start":308.82,"end":324.15,"words":[[308.91,309.04],[309.04,309.38],[309.38,309.51],[309.51,309.98],[309.98,310.38],[310.38,310.51],[310.51,310.85],[310.85,311.05],[311.05,311.38],[311.38,311.79],[311.79,313.59],[313.83,314.3],[314.3,314.36],[314.36,314.56],[314.56,315.57],[315.57,315.64],[315.64,316.17],[316.17,316.84],[317.07,317.41],[317.41,317.61],[317.61,317.88],[317.88,318.28],[318.28,318.48],[318.48,319.55],[319.55,319.82],[319.82,319.89],[319.89,320.35],[320.35,320.49],[320.49,320.82],[320.82,320.96],[320.96,321.56],[321.56,321.89],[321.89,322.03],[322.03,322.56],[322.56,322.7],[322.7,322.9],[322.9,323.77]]},{"el":"s5","text":"En los Casos Insulares (1901), la Corte Suprema llamó a Puerto Rico “extranjero … en un sentido doméstico”; sus residentes son ciudadanos de EE. UU. que todavía no pueden votar por el presidente.","start":324.5,"end":338.13,"words":[[324.59,324.73],[324.73,324.94],[324.94,325.29],[325.29,325.91],[325.91,327.16],[327.4,327.54],[327.54,327.89],[327.89,328.38],[328.38,328.65],[328.65,328.72],[328.72,329.14],[329.14,329.42],[329.42,330.18],[330.18,330.25],[330.25,330.39],[330.39,330.53],[330.53,331.01],[331.01,331.71],[331.95,332.16],[332.16,332.85],[332.85,333.06],[333.06,333.75],[333.75,333.89],[333.89,334.1],[334.45,334.65],[335.0,335.14],[335.14,335.69],[335.69,335.83],[335.83,336.25],[336.25,336.6],[336.6,336.8],[336.8,336.94],[336.94,337.71]]},{"el":"h6","text":"El patrón común","start":339.03,"end":340.23,"words":[[339.17,339.33],[339.33,339.79],[339.79,340.18]]},{"el":"s6","text":"A lo largo de cinco siglos y en todos los imperios aparecen las mismas herramientas: reclamar la tierra (el “descubrimiento”), clasificar a las personas por ascendencia o color, tomar su trabajo, escribirlo en la ley, justificarlo con la religión y luego con la ciencia, y dividir a los colonizados entre sí.","start":340.93,"end":360.49,"words":[[341.01,341.08],[341.08,341.22],[341.22,341.57],[341.57,341.71],[341.71,342.07],[342.07,342.49],[342.49,342.56],[342.56,342.7],[342.7,343.05],[343.05,343.26],[343.26,343.82],[343.82,344.39],[344.39,344.6],[344.6,345.02],[345.02,345.79],[346.04,346.6],[346.6,346.74],[346.74,347.1],[347.1,347.24],[347.24,348.29],[348.54,349.24],[349.24,349.31],[349.31,349.52],[349.52,350.09],[350.09,350.3],[350.3,351.0],[351.0,351.07],[351.07,351.49],[351.74,352.09],[352.09,352.23],[352.23,352.79],[353.04,353.74],[353.74,353.88],[353.88,354.02],[354.02,354.31],[354.55,355.4],[355.4,355.61],[355.61,355.75],[355.75,356.31],[356.31,356.38],[356.38,356.73],[356.73,356.94],[356.94,357.08],[357.08,357.65],[357.89,357.96],[357.96,358.46],[358.46,358.53],[358.53,358.74],[358.74,359.51],[359.51,359.86],[359.86,360.07]]},{"el":"s6","text":"La resistencia también aparece en todas partes, desde el rey del Congo hasta los revolucionarios de Haití y la reina de Hawái.","start":360.84,"end":368.61,"words":[[360.96,361.1],[361.1,361.86],[361.86,362.34],[362.34,362.82],[362.82,362.95],[362.95,363.3],[363.3,363.78],[364.02,364.36],[364.36,364.5],[364.5,364.7],[364.7,364.91],[364.91,365.25],[365.25,365.53],[365.53,365.73],[365.73,366.76],[366.76,366.9],[366.9,367.17],[367.17,367.24],[367.24,367.38],[367.38,367.72],[367.72,367.86],[367.86,368.2]]},{"el":"s6","text":"El resto de los módulos de Aprende sigue estas herramientas dentro de las instituciones estadounidenses.","start":368.96,"end":374.46,"words":[[369.06,369.18],[369.18,369.47],[369.47,369.58],[369.58,369.76],[369.76,370.17],[370.17,370.28],[370.28,370.69],[370.69,370.92],[370.92,371.21],[371.21,371.8],[371.8,372.15],[372.15,372.26],[372.26,372.44],[372.44,373.19],[373.19,374.13]]}]}